# Keep the build context to what docker/Dockerfile actually COPYs.
#
# data/ matters most: the dev stack keeps Postgres, Redis and the blob store
# under ./data/<volume>, and Postgres's files there aren't readable by the
# user running `docker build` on Linux — without this, the build fails
# sending its context. The restricted corpus (CLAUDE.md §6) and real
# inventory/tracker files must never be sent to a build either.
data/
Advisory/
Inventory/
Test_Files/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
.git/
.github/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
docs/
tests/
.DS_Store
